## 2025-02-15 - Fixed diagonal traversals

**What was found:** The `canTraverse` method in `WorldPlane` used `Math.max(Math.abs(deltaX), Math.abs(deltaY)) !== 1` to check for valid single-step traversals. This Chebyshev distance metric incorrectly allowed diagonal movement across planes and wrapping seams.

**Action:** Updated the conditional check to use Manhattan distance (`Math.abs(deltaX) + Math.abs(deltaY) !== 1`), strictly enforcing orthogonal traversals as required by the Dark War engine constraints.

**Prevention:** Always use Manhattan distance when validating cardinal-only grid traversal limits. Verify the traversal logic with differential tests that specifically target diagonal cases across seams and on flat terrain.
